<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC "-//W3C//DTD HTML 4.01 Transitional//EN">

<html>
  <head>
    <title>Hearts - A game where you better don't get them</title>
    <meta name="description" content="Documentation of the Hearts cardgame">
    <meta name="keywords" content="Documentation, Docu, Hearts; game, card, cardgame">

    <meta name="DC.Creator" content="Markus Schwab">
    <meta name="DC.Date" content="2002-12-31">
    <meta name="DC.Rights" content="Anticopyright (A) 2002, distributed under the GNU Free Documentation License">
  </head>

  <body>
    <h1 align="center">Hearts</h1>
    <hr size=2>
    <p>Hearts is a game included with some version(s) of a quite popular
      operating system. Enough said about where I got the idea for it ...</p>

    <p>Every one of the four players start with thirteen cards. The goal is either to
      get rid of them without getting any of the hearts or the queen of spades
      or to collect all of them.</p>

    <p>The game is started by selecting three cards which should be given to some
      other player (except every fourth turn, where one don't exchange cards).
      After that exchange it starts the player having the two of clubs (with
      exactly that card).</p>

    <p>The player continue clockwise. At the end of the turn the player who played
      the highest card (with the colour of the first one) gets the played pile
      starts the next turn.</p>

    <p>If there are no cards left the number of (bad) points are counted. Each
      heart counts as one point and the queen of spade counts thirteen points. If a
      player happens to have got all of them (and therefore would have 26
      points), the score is reversed, meaning he got 0 points and all of the
      others 26.</p>

    <p>The game ends (or restarts), if one of the player reaches 100 points.</p>

    <p>There are a few rules during the game:</p>

    <ul>
      <li>The played card must have the same colour as the first played one (if
        available).</li>
      <li>A turn can not be started with a heart, if they haven't been played
        before.</li>
      <li>In the first turn neither the queen of spades nor a heart can be
        played.</li>
    </ul>

    <p>The player having the least points when one reaches 100 points has won.</p>

    <p>The status line gives some information about what's going on!</p>

    <h2>Note to the layout</h2>
    <p>After starting a game you have (from left to right and from top to
      bottom):</p>

    <ul>
      <li>The cards of the human player. On top his won cards, below the cards in
        his hand. The won cards can be inspected by clicking on them;
        right-clicking allows to sort them.</li>
      <li>In the next line it's the same with computer players 3 and 1. In
        between them there's the played pile.</li>
      <li>In the last line there are the cards of computer player 2</li>
    </ul>

    <hr size=2 noshade>
